    "summary": "Cloth (woman’s weave), a single width hand-woven from European machine-spun cotton. The warp is of terracotta colour, interspersed with yellow threads; the weft cannot be seen. The design is created by discontinuous weft supplementary floats, arranged in eleven bands across the cloth. Six of these are primarily linear in white and blue thread; the other five have float motifs of diamonds, triangles and stars. The warp ends have been twisted into a fringe.",
